<!--
  The harness launcher's foreground: a layer added to the DHIS2 stack.

  The stack is the Capture App's real glyph — the three paths from its own
  ic_launcher_foreground.xml, unmodified, only scaled down and pushed lower to make room. The solid
  layer floating above it is the addition, and it is the whole mark: this is the app that hosts a
  plugin, not the app itself.

  The outer group's 0.69 scale and 44.795/44.98 offset are the host's too, which is what keeps the
  composition inside the adaptive icon's 66dp safe circle without guessing at it.

  Glyph only, on transparency, so the <monochrome> entry in mipmap-anydpi/ic_launcher.xml renders a
  real themed-icon silhouette. The host's own foreground carries its background gradient inside it
  and therefore cannot.
-->
